@startuml
title PayLink - Payment State Diagram
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> Initiated : payment request accepted

state Initiated
state FundsHeld
state SentToBiller
state Unknown
state Failed
state Completed
state Rejected
state Refunded

Initiated --> FundsHeld : fraud approved / funds available\n[hold succeeds]
Initiated --> Rejected : fraud rejected or insufficient funds

FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : submit payment to biller

SentToBiller --> Completed : biller confirms success\n[capture held funds]
SentToBiller --> Failed : biller definitively refuses
SentToBiller --> Unknown : no response within 10 seconds\n[keep funds held]

Unknown --> Completed : late callback / status inquiry /\nreconciliation confirms success\n[capture held funds]
Unknown --> Failed : authoritative refusal or\nreconciliation confirms no payment

Rejected --> [*]
Completed --> [*]
Failed --> Refunded : release held funds exactly once
Refunded --> [*]

note right of Initiated
    Validate amount: 5..10,000 EGP.
    Check account, daily limit and velocity.
    User-approved AQ-14: velocity counts payment initiation attempts,
    including attempts later rejected (2026-11-25).
    Rationale: prevent rapid activity evading the rule through rejected outcomes.
    Basic daily limit: 5,000 EGP.
    Verified daily limit: 30,000 EGP.
end note

note right of Unknown
    Funds remain held.
    User-approved AQ-15 (2026-11-25): inquiries at +1, +5, +15 minutes from Unknown entry.
    Rationale: deterministic retry times from the start of the unresolved state.
    This records user approval, not team/TA approval.
    Never resubmit the payment.
    If still unresolved, remain Unknown until
    definitive callback or reconciliation evidence.
end note

note bottom of Failed
    A definitive failure enters Failed. The atomic hold release
    then performs the required Failed -> Refunded transition.
end note

note bottom of Completed
    Terminal under the official payment lifecycle. FR-27 is a
    separate optional refund workflow; its effect on payment state
    is unresolved (AQ-07) and must not add a lifecycle transition.
end note

note right of FundsHeld
    Hold the full customer total: bill amount plus service fee.
    Sara's example holds 352.50 EGP (350.00 + 2.50).
end note

@enduml
